1. Scope and definitions

This license applies to the Labtune code, documentation, examples, templates,
and other copyrightable material made available under it (the "Software").
Identified third-party material remains subject to its own license. Each
copyright holder grants only the rights that holder has authority to grant.

"Qualifying Economy" means an economy classified as low-income or
lower-middle-income in the World Bank's official Country and Lending
Groups income classification in force at the time of use. Economies
classified as upper-middle-income or high-income, and unclassified
economies, do not qualify. The classification is published at:
https://datahelpdesk.worldbank.org/knowledgebase/articles/906519-world-bank-country-and-lending-groups
The income group, rather than a regional, lending, or other grouping,
determines eligibility. If the classification or an institution's location
cannot be established, separate written permission is required.

"Eligible Academic Institution" means a public or nonprofit university,
college, or comparable educational institution legally recognized by the
competent educational authority, whose primary mission is education and
public-interest academic research or research training. Its departments and
research centers qualify only while genuinely part of, or owned and
controlled by, that institution and subject to its independent academic
governance. The institution must be legally established and genuinely
headquartered in a Qualifying Economy, with its principal educational
and academic-research operations there. A local registration, postal
address, campus, affiliate, or intermediary does not make an otherwise
ineligible institution eligible. An organization or unit excluded by
section 4 cannot qualify.

"Authorized Academic User" means a currently enrolled student, faculty or
staff member, or formally appointed researcher acting solely on behalf of
an Eligible Academic Institution for its Permitted Academic Research.
An appointment, enrollment, or university account grants no permission for
work on behalf of another employer, client, or commercial beneficiary.

"Commercial Entity" means a for-profit business, commercial research
organization, company, or an entity acting on behalf of one in connection
with the Software or project. "Control"
means the direct or indirect ability, alone or jointly with others, to
direct or decisively influence governance, management, budgets, staffing,
research priorities, publication, or intellectual-property arrangements.
Control can arise from ownership, voting or appointment rights, contracts,
funding dependency, or other arrangements, including control exercised
through an intermediary. A donation satisfying section 5 does not by
itself constitute Control.

"Permitted Academic Research" means noncommercial academic or scientific
investigation, research training, experimentation, reproduction of results,
or validation of findings, conducted by an Eligible Academic Institution
under its own independent academic direction and for its educational or
public-interest research mission. The institution must retain control of
the research agenda, conduct, and results and freedom to publish, subject
to applicable law, research ethics, and privacy obligations. The work must
not be performed on behalf of, commissioned by, or operated primarily as
research capacity for a Commercial Entity. Section 5 also applies to its
funding and sponsor arrangements.

"Commercial Use" includes use for commercial advantage, business operations,
commercial deployment, or monetary compensation; internal or commissioned
R&D intended to support a commercial product, service, or business; selling
or commercially licensing the Software; or offering its functionality as
a commercial hosted service. A use can be commercial even if access to the
Software is free. Ordinary academic salaries, public or independent
charitable research grants, and donations permitted by section 5 do not
by themselves make otherwise Permitted Academic Research commercial.

2. Free permission for eligible academic research

Only an Eligible Academic Institution or an Authorized Academic User
receives permission under this license. Subject to these terms, each
copyright holder grants such a recipient a worldwide, nonexclusive,
royalty-free copyright license to use, execute, copy, study, and modify
the Software solely for Permitted Academic Research. No license fee is
payable for these permitted uses. No institution-wide permission for
other activities, partners, affiliates, or clients is granted.

Eligibility follows the institution and the project, not a user's
nationality or the location of a computer or general-purpose service.
An institution outside a Qualifying Economy, and any other ineligible
user or activity, requires a separate written license before use.
Contact Goran Mitevski on behalf of Pioneertown B.V. using section 10.

3. Copies, changes, and redistribution

You may share original or modified copies for Permitted Academic Research,
without charging a license fee for the Software. Every copy or substantial
portion you share must include this license and retain applicable copyright,
attribution, and third-party notices. Identify changes you make. Changes to
the Software that you distribute must be offered under these same terms;
you may not remove or weaken the institutional-eligibility, geographic,
academic-research, noncommercial, or anti-circumvention restrictions.
Recipients obtain rights to the original Software directly from its
copyright holders only if they qualify under this license. Access to a
publicly shared copy creates no
permission for an ineligible recipient to use the Software.

4. Excluded organizations, projects, and indirect use

No rights are granted to the organizations or for the activities below:

(a) a company research lab, startup, commercial consultancy, for-profit
    educational institution, commercial joint venture, or commercial
    subsidiary or spinout, including one owned by a university;
(b) a lab, institute, foundation, nonprofit, center, or other unit that is
    Controlled by a Commercial Entity, acts on its behalf, or operates
    primarily as its research or development capacity, even if nominally
    independent or hosted by an Eligible Academic Institution;
(c) Commercial Use, commissioned company research, or research conducted
    to provide dedicated services, proprietary deliverables, development
    work, or other privileged commercial benefits to a Commercial Entity;
(d) use through a university account, academic appointment, student,
    contractor, intermediary, affiliate, or shared infrastructure to
    obtain for an ineligible entity rights it could not obtain directly;
(e) an institution that does not meet the geographic requirements in
    section 1, including use on its behalf through an institution,
    campus, affiliate, researcher, or intermediary in a Qualifying Economy.

These exclusions apply according to the actual governance, funding, work,
and beneficiary arrangements. An academic name, nonprofit or charitable
registration, educational email address, university affiliation, public
paper, or acknowledgement of Labtune does not by itself establish eligibility.
General benefits a company obtains from research findings available to
the public on equal terms do not by themselves constitute privileged
commercial benefits or make the company an eligible user of the Software.

Use outside this license requires a separate written license from the
relevant copyright holders before it begins. Eligible institutions must
not lend, transfer, or extend their permissions to excluded organizations.

5. Funding and unrestricted donations

Funding or in-kind support from a Commercial Entity is permitted only as
a genuinely unrestricted donation to an Eligible Academic Institution.
There must be no linked agreement, side arrangement, or indirect condition
that gives the donor or another Commercial Entity:

(a) Control or direction over the institution, lab, project, research
    agenda, staff, or allocation of research resources;
(b) commissioned research, dedicated research capacity, services,
    proprietary deliverables, or work for its commercial R&D;
(c) exclusive, preferential, or advance access to research data, findings,
    Software changes, or other results, beyond what the public receives;
(d) ownership, a license, an option, a first-refusal right, or any other
    preferential right in research intellectual property or results; or
(e) a publication veto, approval right, or a right to restrict or delay
    publication for commercial advantage.

Passing support through a foundation, nonprofit, university affiliate, or
other intermediary does not avoid these conditions. A permissible donation
cannot make an otherwise excluded organization or project eligible.
Ordinary donor acknowledgement, without any of the rights or benefits
above, does not by itself make a donation restricted.

Eligible institutions may purchase general-purpose computing, model APIs,
equipment, and other ancillary technical services for their own research.
Such purchases grant the supplier no independent right to use the Software
or to operate the project as its own research capacity. External service
and data terms still apply.

6. Continuing eligibility

Institutional and project eligibility must hold throughout each use.
This includes the World Bank income classification and the institution's
genuine headquarters and principal operations. If an economy ceases to
qualify, free permission for further use ends; a separate written license
is required to continue. If your affiliation, governance, funding, project,
or beneficiary arrangements cease to meet these terms, permission for
further use ends.
You must be able, on a reasonable request from the relevant copyright
holders, to substantiate eligibility through reasonable evidence of
institutional status, geographic eligibility, academic affiliation,
governance, and project funding and rights arrangements. No automatic
permission for uncertain cases or exception based only on an institution's
title is granted; obtain separate
written permission if you cannot establish eligibility.

7. Research results and other terms

You may publish and share findings from Permitted Academic Research.
This license does not claim rights in your research data, findings, or
independently created outputs merely because you used the Software. Any
copyrightable part of the Software included in an output remains subject
to this license. Separate data, dependency, model-provider, and service terms
continue to apply; this license does not grant rights in those materials or
services and does not pay their fees.

8. Reserved rights and termination

Rights not expressly granted are reserved. No trademark rights are granted.
Nothing in this license limits rights you have under applicable law that
cannot be restricted by license. Your permissions under this license end
automatically if you breach its terms; you must then stop activities that
require those permissions. Reinstatement requires written permission from
the relevant copyright holders. The eligibility, noncommercial, and
anti-circumvention restrictions and the following warranty and liability
terms continue to apply after termination.

